# .claude/ mixes two kinds of file: process residue (agent memory, session
# logs, scratch worktrees) and project contract (the development charter,
# the rule cards, the hook wiring, the design record). Only the residue is
# ignorable. The contract is what the next checkout has to arrive with —
# CLAUDE.md calls itself the file every agent must read first, and it lived
# outside version control long enough for a hook wiring to be lost with a
# session; sim-guard.sh records the same fate for its own earlier self.
#
# Pattern: ignore everything under it, then re-include the contract. Note
# `.claude/*` and not `.claude/` — the trailing-slash form makes every path
# inside untrackable, negations included, because git skips the subtree
# without ever reading the exceptions.
#
# settings.local.json stays ignored on purpose: personal overrides.
.claude/*
!.claude/rfcs/
!.claude/rfcs/**
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/rule/
!.claude/rule/**
!.claude/settings.json
.DS_Store


.env
.env.local
.idea/
.scratch/
.smix/
.smix/runner/
.smix/trace/
.vitest
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
*.xcuserstate
**/xcuserdata/
# dhat heap profile output (manually-generated via examples/dhat_profile.rs)
# JetBrains
# Session / scratch artifacts (never commit)
# Swift / Xcode build products (user committed xcodeproj per release decision)
# Build artifact ignores
android-runner/.gradle/
android-runner/.kotlin/
android-runner/app/.cxx/
android-runner/app/build/
android-runner/build/
android-runner/local.properties
coverage
dhat-heap.json
dist
examples/_scratch/
node_modules
swift-bridge/.build/
swift-bridge/build/
target/
# Root SwiftPM build artifacts
.build/
.swiftpm/
docs/ai-guide/insight-*.md
docs/ai-guide/gol-611-*.md
.smoke-passed-at

# Python bytecode from dev scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# cargo-fuzz run artifacts — regenerated on every fuzz-smoke run
crates/*/fuzz/corpus/
crates/*/fuzz/artifacts/
